    {
      "text": "every man walks in his own way, D&C 1:16. go thy way, and sin no more, D&C 24:2 (6:35; 82:7). prepare way of the Lord, D&C 33:10 (34:6; 35:4; 39:20; 45:9; 65:1; 77:12; 133:17). word preached by some other way is not of God, D&C 50:18–20. elders to journey, preaching word by way, D&C 52:9 (58:47, 63). preach repentance and remission of sins by way of baptism, D&C 55:2. the Lord has appointed way for journeyings of Saints, D&C 61:24. all have gone out of way, D&C 82:6. John to make straight way of the Lord, D&C 84:28. the Lord will unveil his face in his own way, D&C 88:68. the Lord will provide for Saints in his own way, D&C 104:15–16. narrow is way that leads to exaltation, D&C 132:22. wide is way that leads to deaths, D&C 132:25. the Lord will make way for escape, D&C 132:50.",
